<%# ONE KIT-TO-APP LINK'S STATUS LINE (BrandKitApp#status; task brand-kit-applied-status), on the app's page: "<label>
    Applied", "Kit changed" (amber: the kit was saved after the app last applied it) or "Not applied". The title gives
    the dates: the kit's save and the application, after the label in full (the line may cut it short;
    BrandKitStatusHelper#kit_app_status_title). The /logos table draws the same status as a chip (logos/_kit_chip).
    Locals: link (BrandKitApp), kit (its BrandKit, or nil: never saved), label (the brand's name). %>
<% status = link.status(kit) %>
<p class="flex items-baseline gap-1 min-w-0" data-test="kit-app-status" data-app="<%= link.app_slug %>" data-brand="<%= link.brand %>"
   data-status="<%= status %>" title="<%= kit_app_status_title(link, kit, strip_tags(label.to_s).strip) %>">
  <span class="truncate text-secondary"><%= label %></span>
  <span class="shrink-0 font-semibold <%= { applied: 'text-success-ink', changed: 'text-warning-ink', not_applied: 'text-muted' }.fetch(status) %>"><%= BrandKitApp::STATUSES.fetch(status) %></span>
</p>
